---
/** AboutWhy — "Why Credo FS exists" narrative section.
 *  Sits between AboutHospitality (white) and AboutStats (navy).
 *  Two-column layout, light-gray bg, full canonical copy verbatim. */
---

<section class="bg-light-gray pt-32 pb-20 sm:pt-40 sm:pb-28 lg:pt-48 lg:pb-32">
  <div class="max-w-[1232px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Section label -->
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-dark mb-4">Why Credo FS exists</p>
    <div class="w-12 h-0.5 bg-accent mb-12 sm:mb-16"></div>

    <!-- 2-col grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 lg:gap-24">
      <!-- Left: heading + lead -->
      <div>
        <h2 data-reveal class="font-heading font-medium text-dark text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl leading-tight mb-6">
          Why Credo FS exists.
        </h2>
        <p data-reveal="fade" style="--reveal-delay: 150ms;" class="text-dark text-lg leading-relaxed font-semibold">
          I started Credo FS because I got tired of watching good operators get a raw deal.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: body paragraphs -->
      <div class="flex flex-col justify-end" data-reveal-group>
        <p data-reveal class="text-gray-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Ten years working in merchant services showed me how the industry actually works. The cold calls. The contracts designed to confuse. The support that evaporates the moment the ink dries. Salespeople who'd never run a pub in their lives, selling systems they didn't understand to people who trusted them.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal class="text-gray-text leading-relaxed mb-4">
          I'm not that. I've sat where you're sitting. I've had the card machine go down on a Saturday night. I know what that moment feels like, and I know what it means when someone actually picks up the phone.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal class="text-dark leading-relaxed font-semibold">
          That's what Credo FS is built on. Not a slogan. A way of deciding whether to take on a piece of work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
